# Point the SD/MMC block driver's folder at `Flash Disk`.
#
# `Drivers\SDCard\sdmmc` is a complete Windows CE block driver already in this
# ROM -- `sdmmc.dll` behind prefix `DSK`, with the block-driver IClass,
# `fatfs.dll` as its file system and its own storage profile. Given a card to
# talk to, the stock storage stack partitions it, puts FAT on it and mounts it
# as a folder, which is the whole of what KeySoft wants.
#
# The folder it mounts under is `SDMMC Disk`, and KeySoft looks for
# `\Flash Disk`. Both are ten characters, so the name is replaced where it
# sits: no record grows, no offset moves, and the rest of the registry does not
# notice.
#
# The signature carries the `Profile` value in front of the `Folder` value
# because `SDMMC Disk` alone appears twice in the image.
#
# This would stop being needed if the DiskOnChip were modelled and its TrueFFS
# volume readable. It is not, deliberately -- see CLAUDE.md.

name: SD folder
because: so a card mounts where KeySoft looks for the flash disk
reach: sole
at: 12

signature:
  53 00 44 00 4d 00 4d 00 43 00 00 00   # "SDMMC" and its terminator
  53 00 44 00 4d 00 4d 00 43 00 20 00   # "SDMMC "
  44 00 69 00 73 00 6b 00 00 00 00 00   # "Disk" and padding

replacement:
  46 00 6c 00 61 00 73 00 68 00 20 00   # "Flash "
  44 00 69 00 73 00 6b 00               # "Disk"
